        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your patient, a 54-year-old male admitted on 14/09/2013 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray showed pulmonary hyperinflation without evidence of pneumonia. Blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. Spirometry supported severe airflow obstruction consistent with known COPD. He was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy. Vital signs were monitored closely throughout admission. The patient responded well to treatment and was discharged in stable condition. I recommend continuation of his inhaled maintenance therapy and close outpatient follow-up. Please do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "8648-8",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Hospital course note"
                }
